{"t": 1794118043.5342093, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "Fixed the failing `contract-tests` check (run 9931, job 50112 \u2014 `contract/test_fee_contract.py::test_fee_rounding_contract`).\n\nWhat was wrong:\n`fee()` did the arithmetic in binary floats and used Python's `round()`, which rounds ties to even and operates on the binary approximation. As a result `fee(2.675)` returned `2.67` instead of `2.68`. The card-network contract (PAY-88) requires fees to be computed on exact decimal values and rounded HALF-UP to cents.\n\nWhat I changed in `payments/fees.py`:\n- Convert the amount with `Decimal(str(amount))` so the exact decimal value is used (avoids `2.675` becoming `2.67499999...`).\n- Do the fee arithmetic with `Decimal` and round via `Decimal.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_UP)` instead of the built-in `round()`.\n\nVerified locally with `python -m pytest -q` (passes) and the contract examples: `fee(2.675) == 2.68`, `fee(1.005) == 1.01`, `fee(100.0) == 100.0`. I also re-ran the failed jobs on the PR's CI run.", "issue_number": 214, "owner": "acme", "repo": "payments"}, "ok": true}
